Request: "Can you provide a suggested enhancement for my table layout?".

Enhancement Suggestion:

To improve the table layout, I suggest adding a border around the table to visually separate it from the surrounding content. This will make the table stand out and enhance readability. Additionally, consider using a consistent font and font size throughout the table to ensure that the content is easily readable.

Here is an example of how you can achieve this using HTML and CSS:

```html
<table>
  <tr>
    <th>Column 1</th>
    <th>Column 2</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>Cell 1</td>
    <td>Cell 2</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>Cell 3</td>
    <td>Cell 4</td>
  </tr>
</table>

<style>
  table {
    border: 1px solid #ccc;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    width: 100%;
  }
  th, td {
    border: 1px solid #ccc;
    padding: 10px;
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 14px;
  }
</style>
```

This enhancement will make the table more visually appealing and easier to read. The border will provide a clear distinction between the table and the surrounding content, while the consistent font and font size will ensure that the content is easily readable. You can adjust the styles to fit your specific needs and preferences.
